---
import { taxonomyEntries } from "../../plugins/library-content/taxonomy";
import { sitePath } from "../lib/paths";

const policing = taxonomyEntries.find(
  (entry) => entry.id === "paper-human-rights-policing-doctrine-and-hidden-taxation",
);
const pockets = taxonomyEntries.find((entry) => entry.id === "paper-from-pockets-to-portfolios");
if (!policing || !pockets || policing.href || pockets.href) {
  throw new Error("Review the justice reading path when its research-map availability changes.");
}
---

<section
  class="section section-white"
  id="justice-to-capacity"
  aria-labelledby="justice-path-title"
>
  <div class="shell prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">A reading path across Volumes I, II and III</p>
    <h2 id="justice-path-title">Law, time and public capacity</h2>
    <p>
      How do legal authority, the costs of everyday encounters and investment in people fit
      together? Start with the Method, follow two research-map entries, then read the Vietnam/Terry
      synopsis. The map entries describe work in the programme; they do not offer full reading
      copies.
    </p>
    <ol aria-label="Justice-to-capacity reading order">
      <li>
        <a href={sitePath("/research/the-independent-observer-method/")}
          >The Independent Observer Method</a
        >
        <p>
          <strong>Published bounded article.</strong> Begin by separating evidence, interpretation and
          proposed reform.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={sitePath(`/library/taxonomy/#${policing.id}`)}>{policing.title}</a>
        <p>
          <strong>{policing.volume} · {policing.status}.</strong> Follow the policing and institutional-power
          direction. A public reading copy is not available for this entry.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={sitePath(`/library/taxonomy/#${pockets.id}`)}>{pockets.title}</a>
        <p>
          <strong>{pockets.volume} · {pockets.status}.</strong> Continue into working-class time, legal
          exposure, wage taxation and ownership. A public reading copy is not available for this entry.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={sitePath("/library/documents/from-vietnam-to-terry-ohio/")}
          >From Vietnam to Terry v. Ohio: Public Investment</a
        >
        <p>
          <strong>Author working-paper synopsis.</strong> Read the historical interpretation and human-capital
          proposal with their stated fiscal, legal and empirical limitations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Keep four kinds of statement separate</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal doctrine.</strong> Check the court's holding, jurisdiction and date. A stop, a protective
        frisk and the extension of a traffic stop raise distinct questions. Start with{" "}
        <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USREPORTS-392/pdf/USREPORTS-392-1.pdf"
          >Terry v. Ohio (1968, official opinion PDF)</a
        >{" "}and{" "}
        <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USREPORTS-575/pdf/USREPORTS-575-348.pdf"
          >Rodriguez v. United States (2015, official opinion PDF)</a
        >; these primary decisions do not establish the papers' wider social claims.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Historical interpretation.</strong> Connecting veterans' reintegration, policing and welfare
        is an argument to examine, not proof that one decision caused mass incarceration.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Empirical claim.</strong> Claims about lost work time, debt, confinement or fiscal effects
        need their own data, population, period and method. A proposed chain of effects is not a measured
        national estimate.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Policy proposal.</strong> The tax and human-capital models are proposals, not enacted
        rules or independently established fiscal returns.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
